 "notes": "I matched all 230 stations: 199 to an Edwards row and 31 to null. 16 of the nulls are observers' or signal stations and foreign places. The other 15 are lights Edwards leaves out: Tees LV, South Gare, Dee LV, Point of Ayr (Flintshire), Straw Island, Samphire Island, Calf Rock, North Carr LV, Fidra, Holy Isle, Ailsa Craig, Portpatrick and Allonby.\n\nThings to check:\n1. Mislabelled countries in edwards1884.csv. Rows p187r7–p187r12 (Little Ross to Ardrossan) are numbered 1–6 from the start of the Scottish list but carry 'ENGLAND—continued'. Rows p192r14–p192r20 (Casquets to Minquiers) are a Channel Islands list numbered 1–7 but carry 'IRELAND--continued'. The Isle of Man rows p187r3–p187r6 have no number. Scarweather (p185r18) has number '9', probably 89. Bressay's range of 6 miles is likely 16.\n2. Lowestoft. Edwards prints the High light (p182r19) and Lowestoftness, the low light (p182r18), as separate rows. I picked the High light. Check which one the keeper reported from.\n3. Calf Rock and Dursey. Calf Rock was destroyed in 1881, so I set it to null. Dursey Island goes to 'Dursey Head' (p192r11), the replacement light with the same 15 s flash. Change calf-rock to p192r11 if you'd rather treat the two as one light.\n4. Copeland. Edwards (March 1884) describes the old Copeland Island fixed light. The station moved to the Mew Island 4-flash light later. Don't carry his character into 1885–87.\n5. Killybegs (rotten-island → p191r17). Edwards's row covers '2 lights', probably St John's Point and Rotten Island.\n6. Shared two-light rows, used by more than one station: St Ann's (p186r3, three stations), Nash (p185r17), Hoy Sound (p189r6), Maidens (p191r8), Eagle Island (p191r20) and Slyne Head (p191r24). Edwards gives one character per row, so the high and low lights aren't told apart except where he writes 'High… Low…'.\n7. The traps:\n   - Start Point: Devon is p184r12, Orkney is p189r4.\n   - Point of Ayr: Edwards's 'Ayre Point' (p187r6) is the Isle of Man light, so Flintshire's Point of Air is null.\n   - Haisborough: the lighthouse is p182r11 and the LV p182r10. Spurn is the same split (p182r1 and p182r2).\n   - Black Rock (p191r21) is the Mayo light.\n   - Phladda (p188r11) is Fladda, not Pladda (p188r1).\n   - 'Oronsay' (p188r24) is Isle Ornsay.\n8. Dates I inferred from Findlay and the station years rather than from Edwards. South Gare, Fidra, Ailsa Craig and North Carr are missing from Edwards, apparently because they came after March 1884. Selker LV, Anvil Point and Varne LV are in it.",
